  "sharing_policy": {
    "onehot": "Explicit source identity and matching chunk index only; no witness-content comparisons.",
    "virtualization": "Explicit source identity and matching address point only; no witness-content comparisons.",
    "shared_ram": "Adapter supplies a declared shared-address alias; read and write references are canonicalized.",
    "local_product_pruning": "Retained.",
    "mosaic": "Public aligned region and remaining evaluation-point coordinates share initial cofactor tables and dense Eq construction. Every claim and prefix remains bound; no witness-content grouping."
  },
  "stage14_api_note": "The existing Eq-factor Cofactor/Endpoint/prove kernel is exported for the ordered Spice comparison. Existing Twist/Shout kernels and proof formats are unchanged.",
  "stage15_api_note": "Expose the existing Eq-factor known-initial-claim driver for the typed Spice masked-value reduction; arithmetic and existing proof kernels are unchanged.",
  "mosaic_profiling_note": "mosaic.bind_g and mosaic.dense isolate full-layout work from per-component batching. Profiling is transcript-neutral.",
  "dense_bit_scan_note": "Mosaic phase-1 region sums (om-mosaic region_sums) and the packed ring-switch partial evaluations (om-pcs partial_evals_packed) take eight rows at a time when they are dense: om-field subset::subset_sums8 builds the 256 subset sums of the eight eq values and subset::column_bytes transposes the rows so that one table lookup per column replaces up to eight additions. Sparse groups keep the per-bit path. Field addition is XOR, so the sums and the proofs are unchanged.",
  "mosaic_scratch_note": "Dense-row subset lookup scratch is retained per Rayon fold and allocated lazily; sparse groups allocate none. Arithmetic and transcript remain unchanged.",
  "masked_native_domain_api_note": "Expose existing Eq-factor coefficient reconstruction, batch inversion and wire-evaluation helpers for the proof-compatible native-domain masked-value driver. Existing helper arithmetic and other sumcheck kernels are unchanged.",
  "mosaic_prefix_note": "Add explicit verifier-provided low-prefix linear functionals for compact Flock gate layouts. Their ordered descriptors are bound before batching; the packed phase folds small multilinear basis tables and retains the existing high-coordinate scans and ordinary final G opening. Empty functional lists delegate to the legacy APIs exactly. RingSwitch and Ligerito are unchanged.",
  "glue_copy_note": "Borrow addresses in the existing onehot packer and hash public words with identical little-endian framing without a serialized copy on little-endian targets. RingSwitch generates initial field elements from packed u64 pairs; Ligerito allocates its canonical packed table once after RingSwitch, borrows its first Eq fold and consumes it for query encoding. Existing owned/repacking APIs and paired/fused arithmetic remain. No witness table or codewords are retained across the IOP; proof/transcript values are unchanged."
}
